esent in multiple opponent melds ([B2,B3,B4] by next player), so B1+B2 in your hand is unlikely to develop into a useful sequence.\n- No possibility of forming a kong or pung with B1.\n- Retaining **F2** (your seat and prevalent wind) offers potential scoring value if you later draw more F2s (though unlikely).\n- **B1** is the least promising for future development and safest to discard given opponent meld visibility.\n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
