 or tiles already being collected (B2, W2).  \nF2 (South Wind) is dangerous because both Prevalent and Seat Wind bonuses apply \u2014 if an opponent needs it for a pung, it gives them 2 extra points. Discarding it could feed a winning hand.  \nW2 was used in Chi by two different players (next and previous), meaning someone may still be collecting W2s. Only one W2 remains unseen \u2014 very risky.  \nB2 is actively used in two chows by the next player \u2014 extremely dangerous.  \nT9 was discarded twice by previous player \u2014 suggests he doesn\u2019t need it. Combined with only one left unseen, it might be safe.  \nW1 is abundant (4 unseen), no evidence of collection, and not involved in current melds. Safer than W2 or B2.  \nBetween W1, F3, and T9, W1 offers more flexibility for future self-use in chows, so better to keep.  \nF3 is neutral \u2014 not valuable to us, not clearly needed by others.  \n\nAnswer: Play F3"}
